    "stderr": "",
    "stdout": "[{\"type\": \"web_search_result\", \"title\": \"Gray Short-tailed Opossum (Monodelphis domestica) \\u00b7 iNaturalist\", \"url\": \"https://www.inaturalist.org/taxa/42578-Monodelphis-domestica\", \"content\": \"Unlike most other marsupials, the gray short-tailed opossum does not have a true pouch. The scientific name Monodelphis is derived from Greek and means 'single womb' (referring to the lack of a pouch) and the Latin word domestica which means ...\\n\\nThe gray short-tailed opossum (Monodelphis domestica) is a small South American member of the family Didelphidae. Unlike most other marsupials, the gray short-tailed opossum does not have a true pouch. The scientific name Monodelphis is derived from Greek and means 'single womb' (referring to the lack of a pouch) and the Latin word domestica which means 'domestic' (chosen because of the species' habit of entering human dwellings).\\n\\nIt was the first marsupial to have its (Source: Wikipedia, 'Gray short-tailed opossum', https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gray_short-tailed_opossum, CC BY-SA 3.0 .\"}, {\"type\": \"web_search_result\", \"title\": \"Postnatal Development of the Gray Short-Tailed Opossum (Monodelphis domestica): Implications for Metatherian Decline at the K\\u2013Pg - PMC\", \"url\": \"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12980394/\", \"content\": \"# Postnatal Development of the Gray Short-Tailed Opossum (Monodelphis domestica): Implications for Metatherian Decline at the K\\u2013Pg\\n\\nHere, we describe the postnatal development of laboratory rea\n",
